WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.800
The first trailer for "Fast X" is&nbsp;
out and "Fast and Furious" fans sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.340
have some intense thoughts about Paul&nbsp;
Walker's brief but welcome appearance.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:13.500
In true "Fast and Furious" manner, the first look&nbsp;
at "Fast X" confirms that the tenth entry in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:19.020
billion-dollar franchise will retroactively&nbsp;
make changes to fold in a new villain. "F9"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.580
managed to convince fans that Dominic Torretto&nbsp;
had a secret brother this whole time in Jakob,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.780
played by John Cena. Now, "Fast&nbsp;
X" confirms that Jason Momoa's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:32.340
villain Dante is somehow connected to the&nbsp;
family's chaotic exploits in "Fast Five."

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.020
As the trailer kicks off, "Fast and Furious"&nbsp;
fans are treated to a family-hating monologue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.760
from Momoa's character, which then cuts to&nbsp;
the events of "Fast Five." As Walker's Brian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.320
and Diesel's Dom are stealing the giant safe&nbsp;
and parading it through the streets of Brazil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.820
fans see that Dante was there for every major&nbsp;
set piece during the fifth film's finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.920
retroactively making him a pivotal character.&nbsp;
How exactly is Momoa's character connected to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.940
"Fast Five"? Only time will tell. For&nbsp;
now, fans still can't get over how the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:04.500
"Fast X" trailer managed to carefully tie in&nbsp;
moments from "Fast Five" that feature Walker.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.960
"Furious 7" marked the last time Paul Walker&nbsp;
appeared in the franchise. The actor died in 2013&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.760
from a car crash, compelling the creative team&nbsp;
behind "Fast and Furious" to retool his character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:20.340
Since the seventh entry in the franchise, Walker's&nbsp;
Brian has appeared off-screen, retiring from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:25.200
family's action-packed shenanigans. The character&nbsp;
was last seen driving to the Toretto residence in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.700
the final moments of "F9," closing off the&nbsp;
ninth entry in the ever-expanding franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.260
While seeing the character's car was certainly a&nbsp;
crowd-pleasing moment for "Fast and Furious" fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:38.040
seeing Walker via flashbacks in the&nbsp;
latest trailer is making fans emotional.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:41.700
One fan wrote, "Goosebumps watching&nbsp;
Paul Walker," in the YouTube comment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.760
section of the trailer. Another&nbsp;
user echoed similar sentiments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.300
saying their "heart skipped a beat&nbsp;
seeing Paul Walker." It was a similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.500
situation on Twitter. A user expressed how&nbsp;
emotional it was to see Brian again, saying,

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.040
"The 'Fast X' trailer just made me so&nbsp;
emotional. Like, I know it's not the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:59.100
first movie without Paul Walker, but&nbsp;
still [...] can't believe he's gone."

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.860
Another user expressed how the use of Brian in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:05.340
the "Fast X" trailer made them miss&nbsp;
Walker even more. Yet another wrote,

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:08.734
"If Brian O'Connor returns in&nbsp;
'Fast X' I might actually cry."

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:11.340
While plot details on "Fast X" are slim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.794
"Fast and Furious" fans can't help but speculate&nbsp;
what the future entry has in store for Brian.

00:02:15.794 --> 00:02:19.394
"Never accept death when suffering is owed."

00:02:19.394 --> 00:02:24.120
Some fans think that Brian O'Connor will return&nbsp;
in the latest "Fast and Furious" movie. Following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.680
Paul Walker's death in 2013, his brothers&nbsp;
Caleb and Cody were brought in as stand-ins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:34.140
to film pivotal scenes for "Furious 7" that hadn't&nbsp;
been completed. With the help of visual effects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.820
Brian O'Connor was able to join the family one&nbsp;
last time. After seeing the "Fast X" trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:42.180
fans think Walker's brothers will&nbsp;
be brought back. A Redditor wrote,

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:46.260
"I strongly think Brian is going&nbsp;
to show back up via deep fake/CGI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.334
over Paul Walker's brother(s) as body double."

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.920
Another fan agreed saying,

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.340
"I was okay with Brian playing babysitter&nbsp;
offscreen in 'F9' [ ... ] but with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.220
stakes this high it's harder to&nbsp;
buy him not getting involved."

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:59.700
Yet another user echoed other&nbsp;
fans' thoughts on Brian's return:

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:04.980
"Paul and his character were a big part of the&nbsp;
franchise and it'd be a shame to not see him be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.180
part of the finale and at least with his brothers&nbsp;
doing it, a part of Paul would be a part of it."

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:13.920
Other fans think that Brian will show up in a&nbsp;
different, more unique way. One Twitter user&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.900
speculated, "Brie Larson has to be playing Brian's&nbsp;
long lost sister, right?" Yet another suggested,

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:22.560
"Brie Larson's Tess is 100% going&nbsp;
to be revealed as Brian's sister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.760
that no one knew he had because he never&nbsp;
mentioned her a single time before, right?"

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.540
Another user amusingly suggested&nbsp;
that "everyone with blonde hair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.000
will be accused of being related&nbsp;
to Brian until proven otherwise."

